{
  "id": "ball_de_bot_mallorca",
  "name": "Ball de bot and xeremiers (Mallorcan dance music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ball de bot is the family of Mallorcan couple dances — mateixes, jotes, fandangos and boleros — played either by xeremiers, a pair of musicians on the xeremies bagpipe and the flabiol pipe with tamborí drum, or by groups of singers with guitars, bandurrias and castanets, while work songs were sung unaccompanied in the fields. Alan Lomax made field recordings of these strands across the island. The gaita asturiana card stands in for the xeremies and the credited-flute card for the flabiol.",
  "recipe": "classic modern ball de bot and xeremiers, functional Song, iberian branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. gaita asturiana, flute like credited flute unspecified, foundational one handed tabor, classical nylon-string guitar, bandurria, castanets. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
